[526, 527] CLAUDE.md:177 (fixture)
  Confirm coverage via `numPendingTests` (skipped) in the JSON reporter, not just `success`.
> - **Every PG/MySQL container suite MUST own its fixture database.** Both containers expose one database (`meshmonitor_test`) and Vitest runs files in parallel forks, so two suites that `DROP TABLE`/`CREATE TABLE` the same name drop it out from under each other mid-test. That reads as `relation "x" does not exist` / `Table 'meshmonitor_test.x' doesn't exist` and has twice been misdiagnosed as "pre-existing and environmental" — it is a fixture race, and it reproduces 100% of the time when you run the two files together. New suites take a private database via `createIsolatedPostgresDatabase(key)` / `createIsolatedMysqlDatabase(key)`, or by passing `isolationKey` to `createPostgresBackend` / `createMysqlBackend` (all in `src/db/repositories/test-utils.ts`). Never serialize the run (`fileParallelism: false`) to work around it.
  - **Adding a column to `nodes` also means updating the hand-written PG/MySQL DDL in `src/db/repositories/nodes.test.ts`** (`POSTGRES_CREATE` / `MYSQL_CREATE`). Only the SQLite suite builds its schema from the migration registry; the other two use literal `CREATE TABLE` blocks. Drizzle's `select()` enumerates every schema column, so one missing column fails *every* query in those suites (this cost ~92 CI failures in #4250). Repositories that select explicit column lists are unaffected.

